Restore the old Vulkan texture layout after defragmentation copies.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    Defragmentation copies every mip into a replacement backing and restores the
    replacement to its default layout. An already recorded command can still pin
    the old backing after its container is repointed, so that backing must also
    return from COPY_SOURCE to its default layout before later submissions use it.
    Restore it after the copy and before repointing/releasing it. Existing texture
    references keep both generations alive; no ownership or callback order changes.

VALIDATION TARGET
    engine.render.texturedefragmentationgpu retains a sampled seven-mip backing
    across real allocator fragmentation and checks sampled/current contents. On the
    unpatched RTX 4090 Vulkan backend, all pixel assertions pass but Khronos
    validation reports seven InvalidImageLayout errors, one per retained mip.
    ForestVillage Luau/JS client initialization is the production acceptance path.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    Pinned SDL commit: fa2c02bb6e21974a89ea9824bc53c9932abe5f9c.
    Re-point the texture branch of VULKAN_INTERNAL_DefragmentMemory after its mip
    copies and before the original container is repointed. This correctness patch
    applies with private queues enabled or disabled. Do not edit the SDL submodule.

--- a/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c
+++ b/src/gpu/vulkan/SDL_gpu_vulkan.c
@@ -11196,8 +11196,15 @@
                 commandBuffer,
                 VULKAN_TEXTURE_USAGE_MODE_COPY_DESTINATION,
                 newTexture);
 
+            // Already recorded commands can still bind the old backing.
+            VULKAN_INTERNAL_TextureTransitionToDefaultUsage(
+                renderer,
+                commandBuffer,
+                VULKAN_TEXTURE_USAGE_MODE_COPY_SOURCE,
+                currentRegion->vulkanTexture);
+
             // re-point original container to new texture
             newTexture->container = currentRegion->vulkanTexture->container;
             newTexture->containerIndex = currentRegion->vulkanTexture->containerIndex;
             newTexture->container->textures[currentRegion->vulkanTexture->containerIndex] = newTexture;
